  "body": "Fixes #887: ruststep 0.4.0 - the newest crates.io release - cannot parse the empty parameter list `()`, which ISO 10303-21 allows (`list = \"(\" [ parameter { \",\" parameter } ] \")\"`). One dead `DRAUGHTING_MODEL('',(),#10);` entity, which is what HOOPS Exchange writes, makes `entity_instance_list` (`many0_(entity_instance)`) stop silently mid-section; the `data_section` failure is then discarded by the outer `many0_`, and the reported syntax error lands on `DATA;` - nowhere near the real defect. SolidCraft and other readers open the same file happily.\n\n**The fix is one upstream commit that has never shipped.** ricosjp/ruststep@90fdc935 (\"fix(exchange): handle empty parameter lists\", Feb 2025) wraps the element list in `opt_(...)` and lands on upstream main, but the newest release is still 0.4.0 (Sept 2024) - upstream issue 256 is an open release request. So this PR pins that rev with `[patch.crates-io]`:\n\n```toml\n[patch.crates-io]\nruststep = { git = \"https://github.com/ricosjp/ruststep\", rev = \"90fdc9351746f1f1d1e435b88f15371edaaaa14d\" }\n```\n\nUpstream still declares `version = \"0.4.0\"`, so both camcraft-app's `ruststep = \"=0.4.0\"` and truck-stepio's `ruststep = \"0.4\"` resolve to the patched crate unchanged, and ruststep-derive comes from the same tree. The Cargo.lock diff is exactly the two source-swaps (registry -> git rev), no version or dependency drift.\n\n**Please flag if this crosses a line: it is this workspace's first and only git dependency**, against the hard-pinned-crates.io posture in the comment above the pin. The comment I added marks it as a deliberate exception to be dropped when a ruststep release contains the fix. If a git dep is unacceptable: (a) wait on the upstream release (open since Feb, no date), or (b) a small patch-fork under an org I maintain, same `[patch.crates-io]` shape - happy to convert if that is preferred.\n\n**Test**: `testdata/models/empty_list.step` is our box.step plus `#166 = DRAUGHTING_MODEL('', (), #2);` - the offending construct, mimicking the HOOPS export. With only the fixture committed the file fails with the reported syntax error; with the patch it imports as the same 12-facet box (`step_file_with_empty_parameter_list_imports`). Existing STEP fixtures are unaffected because their empty lists are entity-level (`LENGTH_UNIT()`), which 0.4.0 parses - only nested value lists `()` break, which is also why the fixture uses `#166` after `#165` rather than touching real geometry.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test import` - 23 passed, 0 failed, including the new pin.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests` - clean; `cargo check` refreshed Cargo.lock with no other churn.\n- Red proof on the fixture: before the patch, `load_model(empty_list.step)` -> `corrupt STEP: syntax error ... at line ..., in Tag: DATA;`.\n- Real reported file (kept offline - it carries my part geometry): headless `load_model` on it before the patch reproduces the exact `at line 20, in Tag: DATA;` from the issue; with the patch it loads, 164 facets. The 9-line repro in #887 also parses.\n\nNot in this PR, possibly a follow-up: the error-UX half of #887 (say where parsing stopped instead of blaming the header). ruststep's `VerboseError` swallows the inner failure, so that is CamCraft-side work (re-parse entity by entity to find the first failing one) and independent of this pin.\n\nChangelog: STEP files exported by HOOPS Exchange - anything with an empty parameter list `()` - now import instead of failing as \"corrupt\" (#887)\n\nFixes #887\n",
